# Deferred: Item Detail section icons + Event Detail coordination

**Status:** Deferred. Tried left-of-title SF Symbols on Item Detail section headers (ATTRIBUTES, PAIRS, OUTFITS, LINKS, HISTORY); **removed**. Do not re-add unless asked.

## Why parked

Event Detail / Event Add use gray 22pt icons on **metadata rows** (calendar, clock, location, theme, notes). Item Detail uses **collapsible List section headers** with plus/minus on the right. Putting the same icon language on Item headers mixed two patterns and felt unfinished.

## Revisit later

1. Decide one icon system for detail screens: Event **row** icons vs Item **section header** icons (or both, with shared size/color).
2. If Item headers get icons again, candidates used in the brief trial: `tag` (attributes), `square.on.square` (pairs), `hanger` (outfits), `link` (links), `clock` (history). Keep plus/minus expand affordance.
3. Align Event Detail (and Event Add) if the shared language should apply there too — including future event-scoped Redress context headers.
4. Consider Outfit Detail the same pass if section headers should match Item Detail.

## When done

Remove this rule.
